1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,250
Let's set up the game together, one step at a time.

2
00:00:04,266 --> 00:00:05,418
First, the bag.

3
00:00:05,738 --> 00:00:07,936
Put all fifty six stones inside it.

4
00:00:09,066 --> 00:00:10,602
Most stones have a color.

5
00:00:10,922 --> 00:00:15,082
There are six colors: green, yellow, blue, purple, white and red.

6
00:00:16,199 --> 00:00:18,333
A few stones are special and shiny.

7
00:00:18,653 --> 00:00:20,338
They are called Spirit Stones.

8
00:00:20,658 --> 00:00:22,664
A Spirit Stone is not a color.

9
00:00:22,984 --> 00:00:24,690
You'll learn what it does later.

10
00:00:26,950 --> 00:00:30,384
Now reach into the bag without looking, and pull out stones.

11
00:00:30,704 --> 00:00:31,942
That's called drawing.

12
00:00:32,262 --> 00:00:33,542
Put them in the bowl.

13
00:00:35,416 --> 00:00:37,080
Oops, a Spirit Stone!

14
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:40,366
At the start, Spirit Stones go back into the bag.

15
00:00:42,416 --> 00:00:45,488
Draw again, until the bowl has four colored stones.

16
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:49,117
Each player takes a board with five animals.

17
00:00:49,437 --> 00:00:50,994
Ana sits at the bottom.

18
00:00:51,314 --> 00:00:52,722
Ben sits at the top.

19
00:00:53,833 --> 00:00:56,307
Each player also takes six action cards.

20
00:00:56,628 --> 00:00:59,721
An action card tells you what you can do on your turn.

21
00:01:00,833 --> 00:01:03,457
Both players get the exact same six cards.

22
00:01:03,777 --> 00:01:06,102
Look: Ana's row and Ben's row match.

23
00:01:07,233 --> 00:01:09,089
Two of the cards are the same, too.

24
00:01:09,409 --> 00:01:11,948
Each player has two Take One Stone cards.

25
00:01:13,066 --> 00:01:14,581
Lay your cards face-up.

26
00:01:14,901 --> 00:01:17,141
Face-up means you can read the words.

27
00:01:18,266 --> 00:01:20,549
Next, the six Spirit Power cards.

28
00:01:20,869 --> 00:01:23,792
Mix them up, and make two piles of three, face-up.

29
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,564
Put the Coyote to the side.

30
00:01:26,884 --> 00:01:28,249
He waits there for now.

31
00:01:29,916 --> 00:01:31,388
Choose who goes first.

32
00:01:31,708 --> 00:01:32,818
Here it's Ana.

33
00:01:33,138 --> 00:01:35,762
She turns her Take Two Stones card face-down.

34
00:01:36,866 --> 00:01:39,021
Face-down means the words are hidden.

35
00:01:39,341 --> 00:01:41,176
You can't use a face-down card.

36
00:01:41,496 --> 00:01:44,354
This keeps the game fair for Ben, who goes second.

37
00:01:45,466 --> 00:01:46,512
And that's it.

38
00:01:46,832 --> 00:01:48,069
You're ready to play!

39
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:50,096
Remember.

40
00:01:50,415 --> 00:01:52,463
Four colored stones go in the bowl.

41
00:01:52,784 --> 00:01:56,389
Each player gets a board and the same six cards, face-up.

42
00:01:56,709 --> 00:01:59,653
The first player turns Take Two Stones face-down.

43
00:01:59,973 --> 00:02:01,850
Next: what you do on your turn.
